Subject: [PATCH] game: use HW_MAIN_MEM for SystemCard_InitRomArchive header
 mirrors

The function writes a copy of the cartridge header to the DS header mirrors
at 0x027FF000 and 0x027FFA80 and uses 0x027FF00C as its "valid" word. Those
are HW_MAIN_MEM + 0x7FF000/+0x7FFA80/+0x7FF00C. The port main memory is an
ordinary array (NitroPort_MainMem), so the literals address unmapped host
memory and the game crashes at frame 0, right after SystemCard_InitRomArchive
starts.

Define the three addresses from HW_MAIN_MEM under SDK_PORT_3DS; the DS text
is under #else, unchanged. gcc-10 -E -P without SDK_PORT_3DS is
byte-identical to the unpatched file (0 diff lines).

